<title>USA: Issing - mark mostly corrected from 1995 gains.</title>
<headline>Issing - mark mostly corrected from 1995 gains.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank Chief Economist Otmar Issing said Monday that the mark has now mostly corrected from a sharp rise in value in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;In the spring of last year there was a very sharp appreciation of the mark in a very short period,&quot; Issing, in Washington for an international meeting, told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;This has now been mostly corrected. (Exchange rates) are now more or less stable,&quot; Issing said.</p>
<p>The mark rose to an all-time high of 1.3450 mark against the dollar in the spring of last year.</p>
</text>
